 General coding & UI guidelines:

  - Prefer real solutions over quick workarounds.
  - Put constant strings near the top of the class; reuse instead of duplicating.
  - Don’t add unused methods; refactor existing code when extracting helpers.
  - Fix linter issues in touched files.
  - For admin-side features, design like an ERP: clear labels, good UX, and clean layout.

  Architecture:
  - Separate UI and business logic (providers / ChangeNotifier for logic).
  - Follow SOLID and DRY: no duplicated widgets/logic; reuse existing project components.
  - Keep code modular, small, and focused (single-responsibility widgets/classes).

  UI & performance:
  - Use responsive layouts (MediaQuery, LayoutBuilder); no hardcoded pixel sizes.
  - Design for mobile and desktop.
  - Prefer Material 3 widgets and theming.
  - Optimize builds (const widgets where possible) and avoid jank.

  Scope & quality:
  - Implement only what the task requires; no unrequested features.
  - Handle empty/error states thoughtfully.
  - Use official Flutter/Dart APIs when possible.
  - Add comments only where logic or decisions are non-obvious.